Z||000006||theogre||10-24-2000||08:09 PM||||soaking them probly won't help the inside a whole lot. To fully clean them they need to be fed under pressure about like they normally work. It's posible to build something to do it but you've got to be real carful building the cleaning stand. cleaner vapor is as bad or worse than gasoline in both flamability and toxic value.<P>If they were working well to start with I'd put them back together with new o rings then once the car is running hook a pressurized cleaner unit to the fuel rail. It's not quite as good as flow matching and individual prssure cleaning but it works and doesn't cost a grand.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-24-2000).]||||reg||1
